WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.233
- [Instructor] We're told to look

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.120
at the following number line.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.080
In this number line, we
actually have times on it,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.890
so you could even call it a timeline.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.910
We're starting at one o'clock here.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.910
Then we go to 1:15, 1:30,
1:45, then two o'clock.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.820
And it says, what time is
shown on the number line?

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.400
So, pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.070
All right, so the hour I think
is pretty straightforward.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.570
We are past one o'clock but
we are before two o'clock.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.480
So, we know that the hour is
going to be one something.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.750
It's not going to be two something

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.040
'cause we haven't gotten
to two o'clock yet.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.960
Now, what is the number of
minutes after one o'clock?

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.210
Well, we have a hint here.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.090
It's going to be between 15 and 30.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.710
And where would it be?

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.580
Well, one way to tell is if you look

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.950
at each of these tick marks,

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.300
it looks like they represent a minute.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.220
Let's just count.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.000
If we start at one, we go to 1:01,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.140
two, three, four, five,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.028
six, seven, eight, nine,

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:07.090
10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.340
Yep, it looks like each of
these tick marks is a minute.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.180
So, we just have to figure out

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.060
how many tick marks we are past 1:15.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.800
So, we can see that we
can go from 15 to 16,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.465
17, 18, 19, 20,

00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:23.048
21, 22, 23, 24, 25.

00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:28.710
So, we're 25 minutes past one o'clock.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.530
Another way you could
have thought about it

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.530
is each of these medium tick
marks represent five minutes.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:39.540
And you can count, one,
two, three, four, five.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.910
So, that's five, that's another five.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.380
So, this time right over here

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.530
is going to be five plus five is 10,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.520
it's going to be 10 minutes past 1:15.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.300
Well, 15 plus 10 is 25 again.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.450
So, the time shown on
the number line 1:25.

